+
+### The Real Vulnerability: CVE-2026-24842 in node-tar
+
+The actual vulnerability is a **Hardlink Path Traversal** in `node-tar` (`tar` on npm), confirmed under **CVE-2026-24842 / GHSA-34x7-hfp2-rc4v**.
+
+**Root Cause — Semantic Mismatch in `src/unpack.ts`:**
+
+The security check for hardlink entries uses entry-relative resolution, while the actual hardlink creation uses `path.resolve()` relative to the extraction `cwd`. The two resolution semantics disagree, so a crafted hardlink target can pass validation but escape the extraction root at link time.
+
+> Note: The snippet below is **illustrative pseudocode** to communicate the semantic mismatch. It is not a verbatim copy of `src/unpack.ts`; refer to the upstream commit linked in the [Upstream Fix](#upstream-fix-reference--node-tar-not-npm) section for the actual source.
+
+```javascript
+// Illustrative — security check resolves relative to the entry directory:
+const entryDir = path.posix.dirname(entry.path);
+const resolved = path.posix.normalize(path.posix.join(entryDir, linkpath));
+if (resolved.startsWith('../')) { /* block */ }
+
+// Illustrative — hardlink creation resolves relative to extraction cwd:
+const linkpath = path.resolve(this.cwd, entry.linkpath);
+fs.linkSync(linkpath, dest);
+```
+
+**Example exploit:**
+An archive contains entry `a/b/c/d/x` as a hardlink to `../../../../etc/passwd`.
+
+- **Security check resolves**: `a/b/c/d/ + ../../../../etc/passwd` = `etc/passwd` -> passes (no `../` prefix)
+- **Hardlink creation resolves**: `/var/app/uploads/ + ../../../../etc/passwd` = `/etc/passwd` -> **escapes extraction root**
+
+The fix in `node-tar 7.5.7` corrects this by rejecting `..` in hardlink targets outright (hardlinks cannot legitimately contain `..` because they are resolved against the unpack `cwd`). Reference: fix commit `f4a7aa9bc3d717c987fdf1480ff7a64e87ffdb46`.
+
