+
+### Debian Security Tracker Confirmation
+
+The official Debian Security Tracker for CVE-2026-0775 notes:
+
+> "Considered as working by design by upstream"
+
+Urgency for the npm source package is marked as **`unimportant`**, with no fixed version planned — because the real fix belongs to the `node-tar` package, not npm itself.
+
+Source: https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-0775
+
+### Upstream Fix (Reference — node-tar, Not npm)
+
+- **Fix Commit**: `f4a7aa9bc3d717c987fdf1480ff7a64e87ffdb46`
+- **Repository**: https://github.com/isaacs/node-tar
+- **Fix Version**: `node-tar 7.5.7`
+- **Files Changed**: `src/unpack.ts` (and corresponding test) — hardlink target sanitization corrected
+- **Real CVE**: CVE-2026-24842 / GHSA-34x7-hfp2-rc4v
+
+**Note**: This fix is applicable to the `node-tar` / `tar` npm package — **not** to npm cli itself. npm cli must bundle an updated `node-tar` to clear scanner alerts. **npm@10.9.8 already bundles `tar@7.5.11`.**
+
