+
+## Why This Is a False Positive
+
+This finding is a **false positive for npm cli** because:
+
+1. **Mis-Attribution by Original Reporter**: ZDI attributed the finding to `npm cli` because that is the entry-point binary, without distinguishing the vulnerable dependency (`node-tar`)
+2. **GHSA Formally Withdrawn**: GitHub's Advisory Database retracted GHSA-3966-f6p6-2qr9 as a duplicate of CVE-2026-24842, and confirmed npm cli should not be listed
+3. **CVE CNA Rule 4.1.12 Violation**: A dependency version bump does not constitute an independent CVE for the consuming package; the advisory was retracted on this basis
+4. **No Vulnerable Code in npm cli**: The path traversal logic in `src/unpack.ts` belongs entirely to `node-tar`, which npm bundles — npm cli has no code of its own to patch
+5. **Debian Marks as `unimportant` / Working by Design**: The downstream OS-level security tracker reflects upstream's own position that npm itself requires no patching
+6. **npm@10.9.8 Already Ships Patched tar**: The published tarball bundles `tar@7.5.11`, which includes the upstream CVE-2026-24842 fix from `node-tar@7.5.7`
+
+The report reflects a **tooling and attribution limitation** in ZDI's original disclosure, not a real independent vulnerability in npm cli.
+
+---
+
+## Why You Must NOT Patch npm Manually
+
+Manually patching npm cli for CVE-2026-0775 is **incorrect and unnecessary**:
+
+- **Cannot patch what doesn't exist**: The vulnerable code is in `node-tar/src/unpack.ts`, not in any npm cli source file — there is nothing in npm to patch
+- **Backporting is inapplicable**: The fix belongs to `node-tar`, and any attempt to modify npm cli's own code would not address the underlying issue
+- **Risk of breaking npm**: Modifying npm cli internals without understanding the full dependency graph can break package installation behavior
+- **Invalidates version integrity**: Any modification to the npm binary changes its identity and may cause compatibility issues with node version managers (nvm, fnm, volta)
+- **Already fixed in npm@10.9.8**: The bundled `tar@7.5.11` dependency already includes commit `f4a7aa9` — no additional remediation is needed
+
+---
+
+## Real Fix: Upgrade node-tar
+
+Since the real vulnerability is **CVE-2026-24842 in `node-tar < 7.5.7`**, the correct remediation for affected npm versions is:
+
+**1. Upgrade `node-tar` directly (if used as a direct dependency):**
+```bash
+npm install tar@>=7.5.7
+```
+
+**2. Upgrade npm itself (which bundles node-tar):**
+```bash
+npm install -g npm@latest
+```
+Ensure the installed npm version bundles `node-tar >= 7.5.7` by checking:
+```bash
+cat /usr/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/tar/package.json | grep '"version"'
+```
+
+**3. Audit your dependency tree:**
+```bash
+npm audit
+npm ls tar
+```
+
+**4. Avoid `preservePaths: true`** in any direct `node-tar` extraction calls as an additional hardening measure.
+
+**For npm@10.9.8 specifically:** none of the above is required — the published tarball already ships `tar@7.5.11`.
+
+---
+
+## Recommendations
+
+- Mark **CVE-2026-0775** as **FALSE POSITIVE** for `npm cli` — the advisory for npm was formally **withdrawn on 2026-02-06**
+- Track the real finding under **CVE-2026-24842** against the `node-tar` (`tar`) package (not applicable to npm@10.9.8 as shipped)
+- Do not apply any patches or code modifications directly to npm cli
+- Document this justification for audit purposes, referencing GHSA-3966-f6p6-2qr9 (withdrawn) and npm/cli#8939
+- Continue standard dependency monitoring — especially tracking `node-tar` advisories, as a subsequent CVE (**CVE-2026-26960** / GHSA-83g3-92jg-28cx — Arbitrary File Read/Write via Hardlink Target Escape Through Symlink Chain) was reported in `node-tar < 7.5.8` and fixed in `7.5.8` (npm@10.9.8's bundled `tar@7.5.11` also includes this fix)
+
+---
+
+## Summary
+
+- **CVE-2026-0775 does not apply to npm cli as an independent vulnerability**
+- The vulnerable code (`src/unpack.ts`) resides entirely in `node-tar`, a bundled transitive dependency
+- The GitHub Advisory (GHSA-3966-f6p6-2qr9) was **officially withdrawn** on 2026-02-06 per CVE CNA rule 4.1.12 (duplicate) and npm/cli#8939 (npm cli not an affected product)
+- The real vulnerability is **CVE-2026-24842** in `node-tar < 7.5.7` (GHSA-34x7-hfp2-rc4v)
+- The fix commit is `f4a7aa9bc3d717c987fdf1480ff7a64e87ffdb46` in the `isaacs/node-tar` repository, releasing version `7.5.7`
+- **npm@10.9.8 bundles `tar@7.5.11`**, which already includes the CVE-2026-24842 fix and subsequent hardening through `7.5.8`
+- A follow-up CVE-2026-26960 (GHSA-83g3-92jg-28cx) in `node-tar < 7.5.8` was subsequently reported and fixed in `7.5.8` — also already included in npm@10.9.8's bundled tar
+- Debian Security Tracker marks npm as **`unimportant`** for CVE-2026-0775, with no fix planned for npm directly
+- Scanner results reporting this CVE against `npm cli` are a **false positive** due to dependency mis-attribution
+
